From 27112ce248dbbc89151d5f4333b9a40549aeeb13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Shuhao Zhang (Tony)" <shuhao_zhang@hust.edu.cn>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:21:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(spec-decode): negotiate checkpoint-aware proposer
 capabilities (#246)

## Summary

- add a typed, checkpoint-aware speculative capability descriptor and
fail-closed negotiation before device/weight allocation
- distinguish DSpark from legacy MTP using checkpoint markers and
advertise platform proposer identities without importing device code
- expose the resolved contract through configuration, startup logs,
`/v1/models`, Prometheus, and Ray metrics
- add drafted/accepted/rejected, acceptance-rate, proposer/verification
latency, and effective-tokens-per-forward telemetry

Closes #245.

## Non-duplicate check

Searched open PRs for `#245`, `speculative capability`, `DSpark MTP`,
and related terms before implementation; no overlapping open PR was
found. Issue #245 had no competing implementation linked in comments.

## Tests

- `ruff format --check` on all changed Python files
- `ruff check` on all changed Python files
- `git diff --check`
- offline disposable Ascend-image test container, no NPU mounted and no
network:
- 12 passed: capability matrix, `/v1/models` metadata, Prometheus
metrics, and interval logs
  - 2 passed: existing `SpeculativeConfig` ngram compatibility tests

The image lacks the optional `pytest-asyncio` test dependency; the new
model-card test intentionally uses standard-library `asyncio.run` so it
remains self-contained. Existing async tests were not selected in the
focused run.

## AI assistance

OpenAI Codex assisted with implementation, tests, documentation, and
review. The changes were manually audited against the actual DeepSeek-V4
DSpark checkpoint markers and the concrete `DSparkSpeculator`
implementation path.
